A||||5||Mach10||Building an engine in my closet :)||||7||
Z||000000||Mach10||08-16-2001||08:12 PM||||Given my sporadic income... Well, ok, it's constant, but twice a year, I have to drop my pants in front of the University's cashier. I spend 3/4 of my fiscal year making up the cash, and blowing MOST of it on the next 2 payments. Thusly, the only reliable way to build a decent engine is to do it in peices.<BR> <BR>After much tossing back and forth, I'd like to do things a little different. I want to keep the 2.8. What can I say? I like the motor. I don't have any concrete number goals. I'd like at least low14s, but that's not critical. I want to keep some semblance of economy, and I want to do as much of the work myself as possible. I am going to keep the auto-box, unless it goes, in which case I will go to a 4t40.<P>Here's my list of wants. However, I'm a little fuzzy on details. Please fill in my blanks:<P>1)Custom-built turbo setup. I'm planning on the t-3 route. I've got a pretty good idea how to make it work, but I'll need some custom exhaust done. Not a problem. I'm figuring that I shouldn't need to run more than 8-10psi for boost. An intercooler would be very difficult to accomplish, so unless someone has a very bright idea, I'd consider it out.<P>2)Top-end buildup. I've read, and talked to some of the older folks, and I REALLY like the idea of roller-rockers and lifters. The hydro-rollers look cool. Anyone recommend a specific brand? Will this really suck with a turbo-setup? I'd like the engine to spool up a little higher than 5500rpm. I figure the turbo would be happier around 6500rpm. So I'll need better springs/retainers. What kind of pressures should I be looking at? The heads will be ported-polished and the shop, as well as a full valve-job. Any recommendations? The air-flow veins will be left alone etc.<P>3) Cam setup. I want bottom end to last me until the T-3 spools up. I need good boost pressure. I have no idea what cam profile would facilitated this. I'm looking for the cam to fix my low-mid range, as the turbo should cover me nicely on the top-end. I still don't understand cams just yet. I'm reading on it, but it's like algebra to me. I'll get it eventually.<P>4)Bottom end: I have the '86 block. During the standard rebuild, I'm going to have the rotating assembly balanced. Can I have this done so that I don't need the balanced flexplate? I want this thing INTERNALLY balanced so that the damn thing doesn't shake itself apart. This is a given. I would like to lower the compression a little, but I'd like to keep it reasonably close to stock. At least as much as possible with a worst-case-boost of 10psi. Piston type? What's the diff between cast/forged/hypereutectic? Rings will be what my machinist recommends. GM says that the rods are good to 7k. Any thoughts?<P>5) I will design a system to move more air through the engine compartment, as the turbo will be heating things up a little. I'm thinking that a scoop under the car, with fans blowing OUT the vents should help. The ignition stuff will be moved to the (slightly) cooler trunk.<P>6) I need a new ignition system. Any recommendations? I know I need something that will retard timing, so my motor doesn't go Maserati on me. Brand recommendations? <P>7) Adjustable fuel pressure is a given, with a rising rate-thingy. How does that work, and can I economically tie that to my ignition system?<P>8) Throttle-body will be bored out by that guy in MN. I might even have this done before school. Just so I can say that I did.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Anything else to the intake system reccomended?<P>9) Will my current ECM be sufficient for this project? To summarize, a turbo'd, cammed, and ported motor, with screwy things happening to the ignition timing and fuel pressure. Would I be better off with a reprogrammed ECM? going to something with a provision for a MAF sensor? Boost sensor? Knock sensor? I'd rather that my engine DIDN'T go down in a shower of expensive parts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Don't feel pressured to answer every one if you don't want to. Don't even bother to quote me, just slap in the number you're answering. There is no real budget per-se, for this project. Obviously, the lower the cost, the faster I'll have the parts together, and the quicker it'll be done. I'm figuring that I don't really want to spend much more than 3-4.5kCDN (2-3US). Labour shouldn't be a factor, as I'll be doing as much as possible. Again, most of this stuff will sit in the closet until I'm ready. <P>Thanks, guys!||||reg||7
Z||000001||baldlobo||08-16-2001||08:32 PM||||why don't you get this book it might help you out: V-6 Performance by S-A Design, you can probably find it at softies speed shop on wall.<BR> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||08-16-2001||08:40 PM||||I just remembered that. I SHOULD go pick it up. Problem is, it doesn't deal much with FI engines. I leafed through it. Mostly it talks about what GM did AT THE FACTORY. I'd have to read it through to glean more from it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||BC-GT||08-16-2001||10:53 PM||||Dude, it all sounds great, I hope you have a machine shop in that closet as well <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>I just think you might have estimated a little on the low side for expenses. Anyway, good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||08-17-2001||08:32 AM||||At the risk of telling you what you already know (but since you didn't mention it in your list of "things to do"), might want to weld and port your exhaust manifolds.  Low-cost performance boost, although labor intensive -   just the kind of mod you're looking for, no?<P>Also, you said you thought the turbo would be happier (with the engine at) 6500rpm.  My stock Fiero V6's seem to have a rev limiter built into the ECM, that cuts things off at 6000rpm or so.  Something to think about.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Capt Fiero||08-17-2001||11:06 AM||||My Home Page, <A HREF="http://members.shaw.ca/hotrodfiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.shaw.ca/hotrodfiero/index.html</A> <BR> Just check over my page and I think you will find a bunch of stuff usefull.  As I myself did a 2.8, I ended up getting 2.9 liters out of it though. My times in 14.9 without any power adders, so with a turbo low 14 high 13 should be no problem at all.  I am thinking about cheating though for the time being and running a small 50hp NOS shot on the motor.  With the massive torque gains you get with NOS I should have no problem pulling a 13.9  My motor alone power is 190lbs of torque and 180hp roughly. <P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
